messages:
maria: Heads up — Aurora demo stream failing during customer's walkthrough. SSE disconnects after ~7s, client shows 'Unexpected end of JSON input'. They pasted partial frame: data: {\"id\":\"r1\",\"choices\":[{\"text\":\"We recommend\" then EOF. Anyone seen chunk boundary parse issues in webview?

ajay: can you share request-id and sample curl? also which SDK/webview version?

maria: request-id=aur-req-202603, webview=android-webview 88. customer tried both SDK and raw EventSource.

chris: this looks like event-stream split mid-json. client should buffer events until complete object. we had similar with proxies that split by bytes. try assembling and JSON.parse only when bracket balance matches.

ajay: agree. also check if our edge is sending chunked Transfer-Encoding + CRLFs. can we get server-side logs for aur-req-202603 (ingress + backend)?

lena: running local repro now. simplified curl that reproduces the cut:

```
curl -N -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" https://host/stream?req=aur-req-202603
# returns: 
data: {\"id\":\"r1\",\"choices\":[{\"text\":\"Hello\"\n# then connection closes
```

chris: yep — parser sees half JSON. quick workaround in client: accumulate `buffer += ev.data` and only try JSON.parse when buffer.trim().endsWith(']}') or when you get a sentinel like \"[DONE]'.

maria: can we change server to emit newline-delimited JSON per event? customer prefers SSE JSON objects per event.

ajay: server change ok, but we should also harden clients. adding small debounce parser + try/catch should avoid crash. I'll draft snippet:

```
let buf='';
source.onmessage = e => {
 buf += e.data;
 try {
  const obj = JSON.parse(buf);
  handle(obj);
  buf = '';
 } catch(e) {
  // incomplete, wait for more
 }
}
```

chris: also check gzip/proxy buffering — if proxy is buffering, events may be flushed unpredictably. ask infra to check keepalive.

deploy-bot: deploy 2026-03-15T14:02:05 started to eng-runtime (rollout id r-20260315).

lena: infra looked at proxy logs — some 502s and a TCP FIN during stream for that req id. forwarding to eng-runtime.

maria: ok escalating to eng-runtime + solutions eng for the POC. I'll send customer the client snippet and ask them to try the per-event buffering workaround. :thumbsup:

ajay: i'll follow up with a small patch for the Android webview SDK to tolerate partial events. ETA today.

chris: if we can, add a small keepalive ping every 10s to prevent middleboxes from closing.

maria: thanks team — I'll update Aurora and log action items.
